    "Question #: 1": {
      "Title": "Exam JN0-680 topic 1 question 6 discussion - ExamTopics",
      "Question": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "A customer has built a VXLAN using an EVPN signaling infrastructure with remote facilities with VXLAN using EVPN signaling connected to the Internet. The customer notices that the network is completely stable with no protocol errors in the underlay or overlay. The customer, however, cannot pass any application data across the network."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Which statement would explain the intermittent loss?"
          }
        ]
      },
      "Choices": {
        "A": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "A. There is an LACP key mismatch."
            }
          ]
        },
        "B": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "B. The MTU is exceeded."
            }
          ]
        },
        "C": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "C. The routing protocol authentication has failed."
            }
          ]
        },
        "D": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "D. The BPDU protection is invoked."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "Answer": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Suggested Answer: D \ud83d\uddf3\ufe0f"
          }
        ]
      },
      "Explanation": {
        "content": []
      },
      "Vote_count": []
    },
    "Question #: 2": {
      "Title": "Exam JN0-680 topic 1 question 27 discussion - ExamTopics",
      "Question": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "You want to converse IP address space and reduce your fabric management overhead. For these reasons, you decided to use unnumbered Ethernet interfaces for your IP Fabric."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Which statement is correct in this scenario?"
          }
        ]
      },
      "Choices": {
        "A": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "A. The donor interface for an unnumbered interface must have only one configured IP address."
            }
          ]
        },
        "B": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "B. PIM is not supported on upstream unnumbered interfaces in the PIM topology."
            }
          ]
        },
        "C": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "C. OSPF is supported on unnumbered interfaces configured as a point-to-point connection."
            }
          ]
        },
        "D": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "D. Only the IPv4 address family is supported on the interfaces."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "Answer": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Suggested Answer: D \ud83d\uddf3\ufe0f"
